LIS: longest increasing subsqeuence

  subsequece ? 
  means we can skip elements in the array

  eg ; a = {10,3,4,5,6} => ✅ {10,3,5} skip 4 (allowed)
                            ❌ {3,10,4} (we can;t change the position of element)

increasing means strictly increasing = {5 , 5 ,10} length will be 2 not 3 because 5 is repeated and not strcitly increasing.
  
  at every element of array we have choices whether to take it or not . we can only take it if a[prev] < a[i] else we have to skip that element is a[prev]>a[i]. 

Approaches: recursion (do choices hai whether to take element or not) -> dp(memoization) -> tabulation -> optimisied tabulation (to save space) -> Binary search (optimised).

as it is template to use anywhere:

1. Recursion

int recur(vector<int>& nums ,int n , int i , int prev ){ // i = current element , prev = previous
        if(i == n) return 0;   //base case

        if(prev == -1 or nums[i] > nums[prev]){  //prev == -1 means no element in the prev .
            int c1 = 1 + recur(nums,n,i+1,i);   //take that element means yes also update prev = i 
            int c2 = recur(nums,n,i+1, prev);  // no going to take that element
            return  max(c1,c2);
        }
        return recur(nums,n,i+1,prev);
    }
    int lengthOfLIS(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        

        return recur(nums,n, 0,-1);

        
    }
